/* ===================== *
 *     Voidstalker       *
 * ===================== */
@901 = ~voidstalker~
@902 = ~Voidstalker~
@903 = ~Voidstalker:

A supernatural assassin who combines conventional thievery with powers drawn from the void. Voidstalkers channel this energy into their ambushes, striking through magical defenses that stop ordinary assassination techniques.

Advantages:
- 1st level: Gains the Unbound Instinct passive ability.

Unbound Instinct:
The Voidstalker's exposure to the void sharpens <PRO_HISHER> reflexes and allows <PRO_HIMHER> to anticipate attacks before they happen.
<PRO_HISHER> movements become difficult to follow, while <PRI_HISHER> strikes find weaknesses in even the most heavily defended opponents.
The Voidstalker gains a permanent +1 bonus to THAC0 and AC.

- 1st level: Gains the Netherstrike passive ability.

Netherstrike:
Rather than striking at their victim's body, Voidstalkers tear open a fleeting rift into the emptiness between planes, allowing tendrils of void energy to surge through their weapon and into the target.
These supernatural ambushes rend the victim's very essence, inflicting magical damage that cannot be stopped by ordinary physical defenses.

Instead of a traditional backstab multiplier, attacks made while invisible deal additional magical damage, regardless of the target's backstab immunity or the attacker's position.
1st level: +2d6
5th level: +4d6
10th level: +6d6
15th level: +8d6
20th level: +10d6
25th level: +12d8
30th level: +14d8
35th level: +16d8
40th level: +18d8

This damage bypasses weapon protection spells such as Protection From Magical Weapons (requires EEex).

- 5th level: May use the Shadow Step ability once per day, gaining an additional use every 4 levels thereafter.

Shadow Step:
The Voidstalker momentarily abandons the material world, disappearing into the void before emerging at a new location, unseen and ready to strike.
<PRO_HESHE> teleports a short distance away and becomes invisible for 1 round, ready to strike <PRO_HISHER> foe.

- 8th level: May use the Void Prision ability once per day, gaining an additional use every 6 levels thereafter.

Void Prison:
The Voidstalker tears open a dimensional rift around an enemy, enclosing it within a sphere of condensed void energy.
For 1 turn, the target is enclosed in an invulnerable globe of shimmering force if they fail a saving throw vs. spells at a -2 penalty.
Hence, the creature caught inside the globe is completely safe from all attacks, but at the same time completely unable to affect the outside world.

- 10th level: Unbound Instinct Bonus increases to +2 THAC0 and AC.
- 20th level: Unbound Instinct Bonus increases to +3 THAC0 and AC.

- May learn the Void Execution, Mass Void Prison and Netherform HLAs.

Void Execution:
The Voidstalker briefly opens themselves fully to the power of the void, allowing them to channel destructive dimensional energy through every weapon strike.
Every strike within the next round applies the effects of Netherstrike.

Mass Void Prison:
The Voidstalker tears open dimensional rifts around all enemies in the targeted area, enclosing each of them within a sphere of condensed void energy.
Each enemy within a 15 feet area must save vs. spells at a -4 penalty or be enclosed in a Void Prison for 1 turn.

Allies are not affected.

Nether Form:
The Voidstalker abandons their physical form and partially transcends the boundaries of the material plane, becoming a manifestation of the emptiness between worlds. In this ethereal state, <PRO_HISHER> body is infused with the energies of the nether, granting them supernatural resilience and freedom from the limitations of mortal flesh.
For the next 5 rounds, all physical attacks directed against the Voidstalker only deal 50% of their normal damage. During this time, <PRO_HESHE> is also under the effects of Improved Invisibility and cannot be directly targeted by spells.

Disadvantages:
- Does not gain a backstab multiplier.
- May only distribute 20 skill points per level (40 at level 1) among thieving skills.
- May not learn the Assassination HLA.
- May not use Set Snare ability, may not learn the Set Spike Trap, Set Exploding Trap, Set Time Trap HLAs.
- Alignment restricted to non-good.~

